-- N1 example sentences, batch 2: the instant, the failure, and the superlative.
--
-- 〜なり (the moment), 〜そこねる (missed the chance), 〜かねる (the polite
-- refusal), 〜までだ and 〜までもない (there is nothing more to it),
-- 〜に堪えない, 〜に難くない, 〜極まりない, 〜の至り and 〜の極み.
--
-- SKIPPED: 〜を余儀なくされる (slug wo-yoginaku-sareru) is NOT in this seed.
-- 余儀 is not a published word and splits to 余|儀 — two single kanji, which
-- `check:examples` raises as a warning and which would ship as two word-order
-- chips asking a reader to assemble a compound they have never seen. There is
-- no alternative spelling: 余儀なくされる has one. 〜の極み was brought forward
-- from 420 in its place and wo-yoginaku-sareru is left uncovered.
--
-- Two rewordings: その shreds to そ|の (as always), and なければ came apart as
-- な|け|れ|ば, so the までだ example is 電車がないなら rather than
-- 電車がなければ.
--
-- Additive, idempotent, safe on a live database.

